WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.610
Class 3-B?

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.760
Ms. Kuroi!

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.920
Yeah, yeah...

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.840
Hey, Kagami.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.750
Do you like chocolate wafers?

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:36.750
I do...

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.130
Really.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:38.720
Then here.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:39.920
Enjoy!

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:40.720
Oh, thanks.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:43.100
Thanks a lot!

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:44.930
I have more!

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:49.600
I have even more so help yourself!

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:50.560
Wait a sec.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:51.770
Why do you have so much?

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:54.270
Well, you know those toys that come with snacks.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.980
I can never seem to get the one I want...

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:57.610
...so I end up buying a whole bunch.

00:01:57.610 --> 00:01:58.860
Yeah...

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:02.530
Some people just want the toys and ignore the snacks.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:07.910
Fox.

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:09.660
Um...

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:10.540
Squirrel.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:11.040
Dog.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:14.880
What are you babbling about?

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:15.500
Oh.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.760
Just wondering what kind of animals everybody might be.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.800
I like to play tricks so I'd be a fox.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:24.300
Based on her image, Tsukasa would be a dog.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.560
Yu-chan's like a small animal so she'd be a squirrel.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:28.680
I see.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.490
So you probably want to say that I'm a tiger or wolf or something.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:33.900
Nah.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:37.190
You get lonely really easily so you'd probably be a bunny.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.070
Plus, your pigtails look like bunny ears.

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:41.940
That kinda feels embarrassing...

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.030
...so stop.

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:43.310
This is fun!

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.450
Me?

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:44.700
A bunny?

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.200
What about everyone else?

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:50.200
Cousin Yui is hyperactive so maybe a leopard.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.420
Iwasaki-san is all cool and suave so maybe a hawk.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.000
Yuki-chan has that whole white feel...

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.000
...and then she just shouts fluffy for some reason...

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.210
...so probably a sheep.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.350
<i>Fumoffu.</i>

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:03.800
Nah...

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.760
Miyuki-san has to be a cow!

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.310
Around there...

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:10.260
That's what an old man would say...

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.310
We were at Konata's place yesterday...

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:18.360
...and saw some of her writing from grade school.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:18.940
My...

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.150
Is that so?

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:21.360
But you know...

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.280
Konata may look like a sloppy person...

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:26.030
...but she actually saved that stuff.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:29.370
Dad told me to keep that stuff safe.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.120
But the real surprise...

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.580
...was the list of her dreams for the future.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.120
Veterinarian and lawyer...

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:37.500
Regular jobs like those.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.040
Really.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:39.710
Well...

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:42.760
The way her dream changed
every year was definitely Konata-esque.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:44.380
When you look at those...

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:48.310
...you can tell what kind of games and manga I liked at the time.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:50.600
I get it.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.850
That's what it was.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:52.930
Back to that again.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:57.810
Then again, some people put down bride for their ideal job.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.280
That's not even a job.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:01.610
That's cute!

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:02.360
No.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:03.650
And like, Tsukasa...

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.400
I'm talking about you.

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:07.860
R-Really?

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.410
This is why airheads are hopeless.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:09.730
Airheads tend to not realize they're airheads.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:12.240
It's not an issue of being an airhead!
Airheads tend to not realize they're airheads.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.540
That may be true.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:15.960
<i>Just so you know...</i>

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.090
<i>That includes you, Miyuki-san...</i>

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.540
Is something the matter?

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:23.590
Miyuki-san.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:26.010
How bad is your eyesight without glasses?

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:28.220
Under 20/200.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.640
Really...

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:33.220
I heard somewhere that eating blueberries is good for your eyes.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:34.640
Indeed.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.480
There are also carrots, which contain vitamin A.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:40.060
Green-yellow vegetables such as spinach.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:43.070
Pork, which contains vitamin B.

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:47.360
And items containing protein such as sesame seeds and liver...

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.240
...are said to be good for your eyes.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:52.490
Also, laster surgery is the subject of much attention.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:57.040
But I'm not brave enough to try it.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:01.260
And I've seen shows about eyesight training on TV.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:03.630
You know a lot.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:06.590
Well, I've only named a few of the many options.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:11.440
But why hasn't your eyesight gotten better if you know so much?

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.680
I haven't actually used any of the methods I know.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.520
Why not?

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:17.640
Well...

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:18.850
I wonder why...

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:20.940
You should give it a try!

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:22.940
Like that eyesight training thing.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:24.070
Right now?

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:25.900
Well...

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.190
First, you close your eyes.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:29.860
And open them really quickly!

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:32.620
Then you look left, right...

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:35.910
...up, and down...

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.120
...without moving your head.

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:38.160
Miyuki-san!

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:38.660
Your head!

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.410
Your head is moving!

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:41.330
Wh-Wha—

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:41.960
Huh?

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:42.710
H-Huh?

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.930
Th-That's strange...

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:47.770
You can stop now...

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:50.260
I may have ended up exhausting my eyes...

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:52.220
Won't that make your eyesight even worse?

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.390
Hey, Kona-chan.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:57.600
What's moe?

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:02.190
When you put it that way...

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:08.400
It's definitely used to express that you like something...

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.570
...but I don't really know the specifics.

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:11.450
What?

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.530
So you use it without knowing the meaning?

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:20.120
I'll just say that anyone who
understands the general meaning is hardcore.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.040
Not that it really matters...

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:23.500
...but I kinda understand.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:26.420
We've got dogs from all around the world!

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:27.550
Otay!

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.090
Puppies are so cute!

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:30.970
Dad.

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:32.980
Let's get a dog!

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:34.800
Hey, Tsukasa.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.600
That's easy to say...

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:38.430
...but can you train it, walk it, feed it...

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:41.020
...and take care of all the other things?

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:43.520
And puppies and adult dogs look pretty different.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:47.110
Are you prepared to care for a living being instead of an object?

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.860
Y-You're right...

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:51.360
I need to think it through...

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:54.710
B-But you sure know a lot about it, Sis.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:55.990
That's 'cause, yeah...

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:58.370
I'm also pretty simple...

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.580
So I went and looked stuff up.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:02.500
Look, Konata!

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.750
You like this artist, right?

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:05.840
Read it.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:07.380
Fine.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:08.630
You're such a pain.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:09.880
Your face is really close.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:41.120
Um...

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:42.130
Do you need something?

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:44.370
I was wondering how far you'd gotten.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:46.540
Did that Osano person already show up?

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:46.960
No.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:49.130
That's still beyond my limits.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:50.090
Come on.

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:51.210
Read faster.

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.920
There sure are a lot of elections this year.

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:55.050
It's killing me.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:55.800
Really?

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:58.680
What's with the gloomy faces?

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.220
Students should go home and study.

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:02.140
Teacher.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.600
We were talking about how there have been too many elections.

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:06.490
Where did that come from?

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:11.110
Election coverage messes up the
schedule for regular programming!

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:14.570
The first airing of this one show was late by four hours!

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:18.200
And then they have updates in the middle of the program!

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:21.410
And the L-shaped ticker just makes the screen smaller!

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:23.080
But you know...

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:26.410
Election coverage is educational in terms of current events...

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:28.850
You shouldn't keep going on about anime.

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:32.380
Besides, air times change even without elections.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:33.590
Stuff like K-1...

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:36.440
...pushes back the regular programming.

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:38.510
Don't you like martial arts?

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:08.910
Sorry for the wait.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:11.750
Kona-chan doesn't have an umbrella.

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:13.750
You could at least check the weather forecast.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:18.680
Maybe I should be like guys and just not care and go home.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:22.720
But I wonder why boys don't mind getting wet.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:25.600
Because they don't have to worry about bras showing through.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:26.770
I get it.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:28.180
It makes sense...

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:30.270
...but don't just blurt it out loud.

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:31.400
Don't you have any shame?

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:32.480
So...

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:34.020
One of you lend me an umbrella.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:34.820
Well...

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:36.690
We go home together...

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:39.280
...so I guess we can make do with one.

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:40.780
Thanks so much.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:43.410
You don't leave an umbrella at school?

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:44.830
But you leave all your textbooks here.

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:46.120
Well...

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:49.160
I had one here...

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:53.460
But I used it once, and I haven't remembered to bring it back.

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.710
It's not a daily routine or anything.

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:58.590
So you only remember if you've made a habit of it.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.300
Hey, Suzume!

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:04.760
Wait up!

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:06.100
Oh, yeah.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.640
When you wear a raincoat and galoshes...

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:11.600
...you look pretty lame.

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:12.730
That's true.

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:15.190
It makes you look like a kid.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:18.980
So why is it so attractive in art?

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:19.990
Like I would know.

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:25.990
Yo, Konata!

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:27.410
Good morning!

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:28.120
Er...

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:29.710
What's wrong, Tsukasa?

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:33.750
I got in trouble 'cause my cell phone bill was too high!

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:38.970
I rarely use my phone so I only
have to pay the monthly access charge.

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:40.480
Really...

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.050
Economical, isn't it?

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:43.970
So you say...

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:45.390
...but if you barely use it...

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:49.270
...the monthly access charge is already a waste.

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:52.560
Don't sweat the small stuff, Kagami.

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:55.990
I got a message.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:03.410
Please buy eggs on the way home.

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:06.170
Understood.

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:08.990
I'll go buy some...

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:11.660
...on the way home...

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:15.090
...with Sis.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:16.790
Hey.

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:19.090
You're talking with your parents, right?

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:23.380
Doesn't it end up more polite when you're using text messaging?

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:25.680
Well, I pretty much know what you mean.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:28.100
It'll change once you get used to it.

00:11:31.510 --> 00:11:33.640
How long have you used this?

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:34.980
Maybe a year.

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:37.310
How long before you usually replace it?

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:39.730
Isn't two years about right?

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:42.860
That's around when the battery starts dying.

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:44.490
I'm going to double...

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:46.740
No, triple that time!

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:47.570
Just you watch!

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:49.120
I don't get the point.

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:51.950
I take good care of my possessions.

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:53.750
I make them last.

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:56.330
You're not even using it.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:57.670
<i>Yeah...</i>

00:11:57.670 --> 00:11:59.920
<i>Some people splurge on their hobbies...</i>

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:02.000
<i>...but pinch on everything else.</i>

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.010
Sorry, Sis.

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:06.380
Can I borrow your world history textbook?

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:07.340
Again?

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:09.810
Geez, you're hopeless...

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:12.970
Here.

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:15.570
Be more careful next time.

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:18.690
I'll return it later.

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:22.610
Your sister's pretty careless.

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:24.070
She sure is.

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:26.570
That's why I have to be the responsible one.

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:29.410
But maybe it's that...

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:31.410
She has somebody to rely on...

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:33.160
...so she lets loose.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:36.620
In other words, your existence allows her to be that way!

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:40.830
That sounds really convincing...

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:42.090
Hiiragi.

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:43.090
What time is it?

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:45.810
There's an alarm clock right in front of you.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:46.590
There is.

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:50.590
<i>A-A victim of Hiiragi's legendary morning violence!</i>

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:51.470
Just to be clear...

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:53.430
It fell and broke.

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:57.560
Tsukasa.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:58.600
You can read manga...

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:00.770
...but you should read the newspaper every once in a while.

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:02.950
It's good to know what's going on in the world.

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:08.290
Um...

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:17.410
Th-The newspaper's hard to read...

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:20.040
I can't tell where the next line starts.

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:23.250
Thought it might be something like that.

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:26.680
You there.

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:27.300
What is it?

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:30.680
Could you call Kobayakawa-san for me?

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:33.850
Tell her the <i>third-year</i>, Izumi, is here.

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:34.640
Y-Yes.

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:36.350
Kobayakawa!

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:39.100
A third-year, Izumi-senpai, is here!

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:41.400
What is it, Big Sister?

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:42.480
Man...

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:46.400
It's so fun how they're suddenly
polite when they realize you're older.

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:48.080
So cute.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:57.590
I wish I could be tall like you, Iwasaki-san.

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:01.090
I wonder why there's such a big difference.

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:03.130
I can't say for sure...

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:05.960
...but it may be because I drink lots of milk.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:06.880
I see!

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:09.590
So it's the result of your daily efforts!

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:10.340
No...

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:12.630
Life isn't so simple...

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:17.900
<i>I was trying for growth of a different kind...</i>

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:21.140
Since it's raining...

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:24.190
...we're gonna play dodgeball in the gym today.

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:28.690
You seem to be the type to be the
last person standing, Iwasaki-san.

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:29.990
Since you look strong.

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:33.910
I actually end up being one of the
last ones left if I'm on the near side.

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:36.200
Maybe it's 'cause I'm hard to hit since I'm small.

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:36.690
<i>They both survive...</i>

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:37.870
I'm not even that good at dodgeball.

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:40.370
<i>...but for very different reasons...</i>

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:40.740
<i>I'd kinda feel bad if I hit Kobayakawa-san.</i>

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:43.710
But I don't really understand it myself.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.130
That's too bad.

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:49.770
We're on different teams.

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:51.770
Looks like we're together.

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:55.140
Iwasaki-san looks like she's good at sports...

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:57.850
...and she won't hold back so it's scary.

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:09.530
I got placed on the outer side...

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:10.780
...so it's okay.

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:12.320
That's good to hear.

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:14.700
<i>Iwasaki-san's really a nice person.</i>

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:17.330
So Kobayakawa-san is attacking?

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:19.930
And Iwasaki-san is on the inner side?

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:21.460
So I'm recei—

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:22.910
Er...

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.170
I mean defending.

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:31.510
I was attacked by infirmary staff...

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:32.710
Are you okay?

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:35.430
You sure are amazing, Iwasaki-san.

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:38.020
You hit one target after another.

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:39.890
Really?

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:42.770
Your movement and reflexes are great.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:43.860
Not particularly.

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:46.310
Oops...

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:48.860
Is she mad I made a big deal about it?

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:49.690
No.

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:51.360
She's embarrassed.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:52.320
Really?

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:54.030
That makes me feel better...

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:55.490
But it's hard to tell...

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:56.530
<i>I see...</i>

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:59.910
<i>So she's the type that's easily misunderstood.</i>

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:01.410
<i>So people who don't really know her...</i>

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:03.700
<i>...get a different impression...</i>

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:07.350
Have you gone on any trips after you got here?

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:09.500
I went on a pilgrimage to all the sacred places.

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:10.210
Sacred places?

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:10.840
Yes.

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:14.090
I visited Japan's three most sacred places.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:16.550
You mean like Kamakura, Kyoto, and Nara?

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:16.930
No.

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:18.390
Akiba in Tokyo.

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:20.100
Nipponbashi in Osaka.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:22.430
And Osu in Nagoya!

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:26.020
And I also visited some sites around here.

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:28.480
You mean like Tokyo Tower and Asakusa?

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:29.650
That's wrong!

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:30.900
Nakano...

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:32.370
...and Kichijoji!

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:33.610
Um...

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:36.750
What's wrong?

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:39.910
I think some dust got in my eyes...

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:41.120
Are you okay?

00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:44.170
Tell me if it gets to be too much to bear.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:45.500
I'm okay.

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:51.310
Good situation, isn't it?!

00:16:51.310 --> 00:16:52.210
<i>No!</i>

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:55.050
<i>I shouldn't look at my friends with perverted eyes!</i>

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:57.720
Hello!

00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:58.220
Hey!

00:16:58.220 --> 00:16:59.010
Come on in!

00:16:59.320 --> 00:17:01.900
I'll go get drinks.

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:11.520
So many books...

00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:13.900
This is all we have...

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:19.820
So Hiyorin once had such a phase...

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:21.530
Kill me now...

00:17:21.530 --> 00:17:24.490
Really, just kill me...

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:26.610
And this would be now.

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:26.830
Oh, sh—

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:29.410
You can tell she's improved.

00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:30.370
You're right.

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:31.880
She's really good!

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:35.970
This picture kinda resembles Iwasaki-san.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:38.590
Takarazuka Revue, huh?

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:40.010
Huh?

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:41.050
Is that me?

00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:43.400
Is this like a fairy tale?

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:48.110
Please let me see it when it's done.

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:50.440
<i>No!</i>

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:53.980
<i>I shouldn't draw my friends in perverted ways!</i>

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:56.280
Tamura-san.

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:58.400
Shall we go to Maiden Road?

00:17:58.400 --> 00:17:59.440
That was the plan.

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:01.570
What's Maiden Road like?

00:18:01.570 --> 00:18:03.840
You don't know?!

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:04.870
Neither do I.

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:06.240
Good grief.

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:08.950
Maiden Road, huh...

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:10.500
Maiden Road...

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:15.090
...is a street west of
Sunshine 60 in Ikebukuro, Tokyo.

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:20.880
Many stores sell manga,
anime, and character goods.

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:24.720
It's as popular as Akiba in
terms of attracting hardcore fans.

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:26.140
However, unlike Akiba...

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:27.640
...the customers
are mostly female...

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:31.270
...which is why it was
named Maiden Road.

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:34.320
In other words, it's a
gathering place for fujoshi.

00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:35.360
Fujoshi?

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:36.820
Written as rotten girl...

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:37.820
Pronounced fujoshi.

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:39.320
They're rotten?!

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:40.030
Well...

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:42.360
That's one way to look at it...

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:57.000
Y-Y'know!

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:59.720
The three-second-rule! The three-second-rule!

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:03.010
If it's under five seconds...

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:04.550
...there won't be any bacteria!

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:05.090
What?

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:07.140
We didn't say anything.

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:20.110
My beloved meatball...

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:23.530
What happened to the three-second-rule?

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:24.150
Well...

00:19:24.150 --> 00:19:27.990
Just let me say that it depends on the situation.

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:35.290
Good lucky!

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:36.380
Okay!

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:39.500
Let's have another blast today!

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:44.300
We've managed to make it to the
eighteenth episode of Lucky Channel!

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:45.300
Okay!

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:48.100
You all know who the navigator is by now!

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:50.390
Akira Kogami!

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:51.350
And...

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:52.060
Yes!

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:53.600
Akira-sama's assistant...

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:56.190
...working hard again today...

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:57.900
Minoru Shiraishi!

00:19:57.900 --> 00:20:00.440
Well, today's theme...

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:03.400
...is the introduction for all of the new characters...

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:06.360
...who have joined the regular cast!

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:07.280
All of them!

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:07.910
Too many!

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:10.370
First, the addition to the Izumi family...

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:11.520
Konata-san's cousin.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:12.990
Yutaka Kobayakawa-san.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:14.700
And her classmates...

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:16.040
Minami Iwasaki-san.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:17.330
Hiyori Tamura-san.

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:19.170
Patricia Martin-san.

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:20.420
In addition!

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:22.090
We have Kagami-san's classmates.

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:23.380
Misao Kusakabe-san...

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:25.260
...and Ayano Minegishi-san.

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:27.930
It's gotten rather lively!

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:29.290
As you may have already noticed...

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:30.430
It's blocking me.

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:31.250
...the new characters have been appearing in the opening...

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:32.600
Hey

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:33.850
I said that it's blocking me!

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:36.310
It went flying!
How many more characters are they going to introduce?!

00:20:36.310 --> 00:20:37.770
We're on the eighteenth episode!

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:40.080
What happened to my appearance?!

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:41.150
That's right, Akira-sama.

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:43.020
Didn't you just make an appearance?

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:46.430
That adorable image of you in a raincoat and galoshes.

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:46.900
Yeah.

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:48.240
What to say...

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:48.950
Last week...

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:51.450
...I was able to talk with our guest, Anizawa-san...

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:53.830
...and he told me that an actor needs initiative!

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:56.000
And presence!

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:56.960
Indeed.

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:58.290
Your appearance today...

00:20:58.290 --> 00:20:59.620
...brief as it was...

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:02.580
...was screaming to me, "Akira Kogami is here—

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:04.260
You sound passionate.

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:07.160
Hey.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:08.140
Yes?

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:09.550
Hey!

00:21:09.550 --> 00:21:10.050
Ah, no.

00:21:10.050 --> 00:21:11.150
It's nothing.

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:12.180
Oh, no!

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:13.810
It's time to say goodbye.

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:14.720
So there you have it.

00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:15.510
We're waiting for you to send us any
questions or comments about the show!

00:21:15.510 --> 00:21:16.360
Hey.

00:21:16.360 --> 00:21:18.430
We're waiting for you to send us any
questions or comments about the show!

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:19.730
Who is it?

00:21:19.730 --> 00:21:21.900
You can direct them to our home page or the radio show!

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:22.140
Then bye-bee!

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:23.700
Turn that thing off!

00:21:26.440 --> 00:21:26.600
Then good work!

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:27.640
Was it a message?

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:27.860
No.

00:21:27.860 --> 00:21:28.230
No, it wasn't!

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:29.240
Was it a message?

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:29.990
N-No way!

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:30.490
Of course not!

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:32.030
Who's it from?

00:21:32.030 --> 00:21:33.240
Uh, it was from my parents.

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:34.160
About what?

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:35.610
Well, they wanted me to go visit...

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:36.830
What was your reply?

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:38.030
Uh, you know...

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:38.790
Say it.

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:39.500
Well, basically...

00:22:56.150 --> 00:22:57.230
Okay.

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:01.130
Kinda screwed up on the falsetto.

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:03.800
Sorry.

00:23:03.800 --> 00:23:05.090
It was touching!

00:23:05.090 --> 00:23:06.040
Touching!

00:23:06.040 --> 00:23:06.340
Shankya.

00:23:06.340 --> 00:23:07.040
Touching!

00:23:07.040 --> 00:23:07.840
Shankya.

00:23:07.840 --> 00:23:09.240
That's so old!

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:13.370
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:13.660 --> 00:23:14.240
Hiyori here!

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:15.410
Patricia here!

00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:15.830
Patty.

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:16.870
Are you used to your job yet?

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:17.250
Yes!

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:18.330
Perfectly!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:19.250
With Patty around...

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:22.750
...first-timers can probably have a fun time without being nervous.

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:23.320
No.

00:23:23.320 --> 00:23:25.460
I don't handle first-timers.

00:23:25.460 --> 00:23:26.420
Really?

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:31.010
I only serve people who've visited lots and paid lots!

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:32.800
It's store policy.

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:34.970
Th-That's pretty harsh...

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:35.640
Next time:

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:36.930
2D has Substance.

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:38.430
Look forward to next time!
